{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Jacob finished commanding, etc.</b> From this you learn that it was not concerning Jacob that it was said (Ecclesiastes 8:8): ״וְאֵין שִׁלְטוֹן בְּיוֹם הַמָּוֶת״ — for the matter was in his desire and within his authority, until he finished commanding his sons as he wished, and only then <b>he gathered his feet</b>, etc. This is the statement of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Ta'anit 5b): Jacob our father did not die — for if death had ruled over him, he would not have had authority until the time he wished to gather his feet. Go forth and learn from what they said of blessed memory in expounding the verse (Ecclesiastes 8:8): ״וְאֵין שִׁלְטוֹן״ — that there is no one to suspend the אונקלומא, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:10.347996919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}